  "description": "Na₂PtO₂ is Ilmenite-like structured and crystallizes in the orthorhombic Immm space group. Na is bonded to four equivalent O atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing NaO₄ trigonal pyramids. There are two shorter (2.30 Å) and two longer (2.33 Å) Na-O bond lengths. Pt is bonded in a square co-planar geometry to four equivalent O atoms. All Pt-O bond lengths are 2.05 Å. O is bonded to four equivalent Na and two equivalent Pt atoms to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing ONa₄Pt₂ octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 0-17°.",
